# Deployment & Hosting

## Production topology

```
Respondent / owner browser
        │
        ├─► Vercel (Next.js)     https://fde-quest-2.vercel.app
        │       Supabase Auth + RLS I/O (Postgres, Storage)
        │
        └─► API Gateway HTTP API (ap-south-1)
                └─► sketch-to-form-api (Lambda, Mangum + FastAPI)
                        │ async invoke (Event)
                        └─► sketch-to-form-worker (Lambda, LangGraph job)
```

- **Frontend:** Vercel project `fde-quest-2` (`frontend/vercel.json`). Set `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` to the API Gateway `ApiEndpoint` printed by `backend/deploy_lambda.sh`.
- **Backend:** AWS Lambda in **`ap-south-1`** — **zip artifact** (no Docker). One zip, two handlers in `app/lambda_handlers.py`.
- **Database / auth / storage:** Supabase (linked project in `supabase/.temp/linked-project.json`).

## Local vs production backend

| Setting | Local (`uvicorn`) | Production (Lambda) |
|---------|-------------------|---------------------|
| `JOB_DISPATCH_MODE` | `background` | `lambda` |
| `WORKER_FUNCTION_NAME` | empty | `sketch-to-form-worker` |
| Job execution | FastAPI `BackgroundTasks` | API Lambda async-invokes worker |
| `CORS_ORIGINS` | `http://localhost:3000` | includes `https://fde-quest-2.vercel.app` |

Local dev: `uv run uvicorn app.main:app --reload` on `:8000` with `frontend` pointing at `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000` (default in `src/lib/api/forms.ts`).

## Lambda deploy (idempotent)

From `backend/`:

```bash
./deploy_lambda.sh
```

Script creates/reuses: S3 bucket `sketch-to-form-lambda-<ACCOUNT_ID>`, IAM roles, both functions, API Gateway HTTP API `sketch-to-form-http`. Re-run after code changes — endpoint URL is stable.

**Build notes:** cross-install deps with `--python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_34` (Amazon Linux 2023 / glibc 2.34). Artifact ~65 MB zipped via S3 (over direct-upload cap). Ignore `.lambda-build/` and `.lambda-build.zip` (see `backend/.gitignore`).

**Do not** use Lambda Function URLs on this account (`AuthType=NONE` returns 403) — API Gateway HTTP API is required.

Full reference: `backend/DEPLOY_LAMBDA.md`.

## Frontend env (Vercel)

Set in Vercel project settings (mirror `frontend/.env.local`):

- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`
- `SUPABASE_URL`, `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` (server only)
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` — API Gateway base URL (no trailing slash)

## Backend env (Lambda)

Injected by `deploy_lambda.sh` from `backend/.env` (secrets) plus script overrides:

- `JOB_DISPATCH_MODE=lambda`, `WORKER_FUNCTION_NAME=sketch-to-form-worker`
- `CORS_ORIGINS` includes production Vercel origin
- Supabase keys, `SKETCHES_BUCKET`, LLM provider vars — see `backend/.env.example`

JWT auth is enforced **inside FastAPI** (`app/security.py`); API Gateway has no AWS-level JWT — do not expose unauthenticated admin routes.

## CORS & troubleshooting

- Browser CORS errors: caller origin must be in `CORS_ORIGINS` — edit `CORS_ORIGINS` in `deploy_lambda.sh` and redeploy.
- Wrong native `.so` on Lambda: rebuild with `deploy_lambda.sh` (correct `--python-platform`).
- Logs: `aws logs tail /aws/lambda/sketch-to-form-api --follow --region ap-south-1`

## Change discipline

- Hosting-only changes: prefer `deploy_lambda.sh` / Vercel env — avoid hardcoding API URLs in source.
- Pipeline or API contract changes: update `CLAUDE.md` / PRD if behavior changes; keep `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` as the single frontend switch.
